<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Betuwe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Betuwe is a region of the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelderland">Gelderland</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, lying between the Nederrijn and Lek to the north and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waal">Waal</a> to the south. Its name derives from that of the Batavi, who settled there in Roman times. It is fertile river-clay land known for its orchards.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/betuwe.jpg" alt="Betuwe" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RACM &amp;amp; TNO · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:50nc_ex_leg_copy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
